<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guy I, Count of Ponthieu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1100">1100</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Guy I of Ponthieu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guy I was Count of Ponthieu, on the Channel coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, from 1053 until his death in 1100. In 1064 he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson">Harold Godwinson</a> after his shipwreck and handed him over to Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a>, an episode shown on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayeux-tapestry">Bayeux Tapestry</a>. He had earlier been captured by the Normans at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mortemer">Battle of Mortemer</a> in 1054 and afterwards became William's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guy-i-count-of-ponthieu.jpg" alt="Guy I, Count of Ponthieu" width="152" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bayeux Tapestry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guy_of_Ponthieu.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
